1
00:00:01,626 --> 00:00:04,045
[TONI]<i> We're all in this together</i>
<i>for LoveList.</i>

2
00:00:04,129 --> 00:00:06,798
<i>For friends who are family.</i>

3
00:00:06,881 --> 00:00:08,758
<i>For friends…</i>

4
00:00:09,342 --> 00:00:11,720
<i>who make boyfriends jealous.</i>

5
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:17,851
[JORDAN SINGING]
<i>♪ Run to me If they cast you aside ♪</i>

6
00:00:17,934 --> 00:00:20,729
<i>♪ And if you've lost all drive ♪</i>

7
00:00:20,812 --> 00:00:25,900
<i>♪ I'll be your solace ♪</i>

8
00:00:25,984 --> 00:00:28,945
<i>I realized that there are</i>
<i>many kinds of love.</i>

9
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:31,114
<i>But all of them are magical.</i>

10
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:35,660
<i>We will give a package</i>
<i>that transforms the entire wedding</i>

11
00:00:35,744 --> 00:00:37,579
<i>into a story unfolding.</i>

12
00:00:37,662 --> 00:00:39,622
<i>How do we fund that?</i>

13
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:40,707
[RALPH] <i>I'll invest.</i>

14
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:42,751
[BILLY] <i>Hi, good evening.</i>

15
00:00:42,834 --> 00:00:44,377
<i>Thank you for calling LoveLine.</i>

16
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:45,795
<i>I love Theo, you know.</i>

17
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:47,130
<i>But there's just one problem.</i>

18
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:48,298
<i>My dad doesn't approve of him.</i>

19
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:50,049
<i>He's just a cook.</i>

20
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,718
<i>I think</i>

21
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:53,261
<i>he just wants to protect you.</i>

22
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:54,512
<i>You know, sometimes,</i>

23
00:00:54,596 --> 00:00:57,432
<i>even love can come out as control.</i>

24
00:00:57,515 --> 00:00:58,892
[ABI] <i>Seriously?!</i>

25
00:00:58,975 --> 00:01:00,727
<i>Can't you see I'm working?</i>

26
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:02,604
<i>So what's the update on your computers?</i>

27
00:01:02,687 --> 00:01:04,355
<i>One of the computers</i>

28
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:06,983
<i>has our pictures and videos on it.</i>

29
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:08,651
[ABI] <i>Seriously, Caloy?!</i>

30
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:10,111
[CALOY] <i>Where are they donating them?</i>

31
00:01:10,195 --> 00:01:12,572
[ABI] <i>I only know of one place</i>
<i>they'd donate them to.</i>

32
00:01:17,577 --> 00:01:24,542
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

33
00:01:46,022 --> 00:01:51,945
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

34
00:01:52,737 --> 00:01:56,533
Miss, do you know my daughter, Bea?

35
00:01:56,616 --> 00:01:59,536
She always comes here.

36
00:01:59,619 --> 00:02:01,746
Oh, I don't know a Bea.

37
00:02:02,914 --> 00:02:03,957
I'm sorry, ma'am.

38
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,125
Thank you.

39
00:02:10,171 --> 00:02:16,928
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC RESUMES]

40
00:02:21,474 --> 00:02:22,976
Which one is it?

41
00:02:31,901 --> 00:02:38,908
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

42
00:02:43,204 --> 00:02:46,040
I knew it!

43
00:02:46,124 --> 00:02:48,376
- This is where Bea goes!
- Auntie?

44
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:50,044
- No!
- Where is she?

45
00:02:50,128 --> 00:02:53,673
- She's at work!
- No. I know she's here.

46
00:02:53,756 --> 00:02:56,885
- Just tell me the truth.
- She's really not here.

47
00:02:56,968 --> 00:02:59,137
She's at work right now.

48
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:02,223
And don't be too loud.
My boss might scold me.

49
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:05,226
- Just tell me the truth!
- I am telling the truth.

50
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:07,228
Bea is at work.

51
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:09,105
- At work?
- I'm just fixing some stuff.

52
00:03:09,188 --> 00:03:10,064
[MARIELA] No!

53
00:03:11,399 --> 00:03:14,777
[APPLAUSE]

54
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:16,487
[PANTING] Ma'am Precious!

55
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:19,240
Ms. Mariela is acting out.
She's hurting someone.

56
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:21,159
- Where is she?
- That way, ma'am.

57
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:22,702
[PRECIOUS] Let's talk to her.

58
00:03:23,286 --> 00:03:24,871
- [CALOY] Please, don't!
- Why are you here?!

59
00:03:24,954 --> 00:03:26,247
Mariela! Mariela.

60
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:28,166
What's going on here?

61
00:03:28,249 --> 00:03:29,250
Ask him!

62
00:03:32,629 --> 00:03:33,588
Caloy?

63
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:38,885
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:03:39,761 --> 00:03:40,678
[JORDAN] You.

65
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:44,265
What are you doing here? Huh?

66
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:46,226
- Don't come closer.
- Answer me.

67
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:48,061
- Caloy!
- Stay back!

68
00:03:48,144 --> 00:03:49,395
[PRECIOUS SCREAMS]

69
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:50,939
[JORDAN] Caloy!

70
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:54,859
Hey! Where are you going?

71
00:03:54,943 --> 00:03:58,488
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

72
00:03:58,571 --> 00:04:00,365
- [JORDAN GRUNTING]
- Come on, hit me!

73
00:04:10,458 --> 00:04:16,130
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

74
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:20,885
Why… won't you…

75
00:04:20,969 --> 00:04:21,928
start?!

76
00:04:22,011 --> 00:04:23,054
[GRUNTS]

77
00:04:32,146 --> 00:04:33,439
- [CAR HORN HONKS]
- [CALOY GRUNTS]

78
00:04:33,523 --> 00:04:34,857
Caloy!

79
00:04:34,941 --> 00:04:40,238
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

80
00:04:46,911 --> 00:04:53,626
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

81
00:05:31,789 --> 00:05:33,791
I didn't want to let him get away, but…

82
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:36,002
I didn't mean for this to happen.

83
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:38,629
I didn't see the oncoming car.

84
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:39,547
Jordan…

85
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:41,549
I just wanted to know
what he was doing here.

86
00:05:41,632 --> 00:05:43,176
It's not your fault, okay?

87
00:05:44,177 --> 00:05:45,928
It was an accident.

88
00:05:48,514 --> 00:05:49,974
I'll go to the hospital with him.

89
00:05:50,058 --> 00:05:51,184
Jordan!

90
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:54,312
Billy…

91
00:05:54,979 --> 00:05:58,066
That Carlos Toledo…

92
00:05:58,149 --> 00:06:00,318
One of our outpatients knows him.

93
00:06:01,110 --> 00:06:03,446
They're also mad at him.

94
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:06,824
Are you feeling better?

95
00:06:06,908 --> 00:06:08,868
What really happened?

96
00:06:08,951 --> 00:06:09,827
It's that guy!

97
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:13,539
He's taking my daughter away from me.
I can't let that happen.

98
00:06:13,623 --> 00:06:15,124
Who's your daughter?

99
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:17,335
Bea.

100
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:19,504
Her name is Bea.

101
00:06:19,587 --> 00:06:21,631
Mariela, we don't know any Bea.

102
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:23,800
We keep telling you that.

103
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:25,551
You're all liars.

104
00:06:25,635 --> 00:06:28,096
If Bea isn't here,
then why was Caloy here?

105
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:30,389
She's the only one he'd come here for.

106
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:33,476
You're all treating me like I'm stupid.

107
00:06:33,559 --> 00:06:34,769
I'm not stupid.

108
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:39,315
[DRAMATIC STING]

109
00:06:41,025 --> 00:06:42,860
[LINE RINGING]

110
00:06:45,196 --> 00:06:47,490
[BUSY TONE BEEPS]

111
00:06:47,573 --> 00:06:50,952
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

112
00:06:52,286 --> 00:06:53,830
In deep thought, huh?

113
00:06:54,372 --> 00:06:56,207
Oh. Morrie.

114
00:06:56,290 --> 00:06:58,835
I was just thinking about

115
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:01,003
our project.

116
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:02,964
You know what?

117
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:05,258
You're impressive.

118
00:07:05,341 --> 00:07:06,843
Oh, really?

119
00:07:06,926 --> 00:07:07,802
Do you mean it?

120
00:07:07,885 --> 00:07:09,345
Yes. No, seriously.

121
00:07:09,428 --> 00:07:10,680
I agree with Ms. Camille.

122
00:07:10,763 --> 00:07:14,058
You're not just hardworking,
but you're also brilliant.

123
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:15,226
You're a gem.

124
00:07:15,935 --> 00:07:18,563
Aw, thank you. Thank you so much, Morrie.

125
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:19,814
It means a lot.

126
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:20,940
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

127
00:07:22,233 --> 00:07:23,401
[MORRIE CHUCKLES POLITELY]

128
00:07:23,901 --> 00:07:29,240
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

129
00:07:29,323 --> 00:07:31,075
[BUSY TONE BEEPS]

130
00:07:34,829 --> 00:07:36,372
[KEYBOARD CLACKS]

131
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:42,503
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
- [KEYBOARD CLACKING]

132
00:07:54,015 --> 00:07:55,892
[DOOR OPENS, CREAKS]

133
00:08:02,523 --> 00:08:03,691
Billy.

134
00:08:04,358 --> 00:08:05,985
Mariela is in the clinic.

135
00:08:06,068 --> 00:08:08,196
She fell asleep from exhaustion.

136
00:08:09,363 --> 00:08:11,282
You know what I'm thinking?

137
00:08:11,365 --> 00:08:15,036
I bet Caloy's trying to steal
our computers.

138
00:08:15,119 --> 00:08:18,581
And he saw how busy we were
with the event.

139
00:08:18,664 --> 00:08:20,625
But Mariela caught him.

140
00:08:23,461 --> 00:08:27,006
But, Auntie Pres,
these computers came from Abi.

141
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:30,510
I think he needed something from here.

142
00:08:30,593 --> 00:08:37,016
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

143
00:08:43,898 --> 00:08:50,655
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

144
00:08:57,578 --> 00:08:58,871
I knew it.

145
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:06,504
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

146
00:09:13,177 --> 00:09:14,303
Caloy?

147
00:09:15,721 --> 00:09:18,015
Ms. Mariela, how do you feel?

148
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:20,851
Where's Caloy?

149
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:22,311
I want to talk to him.

150
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:23,938
Uh…

151
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:26,649
He already went home.

152
00:09:30,861 --> 00:09:34,198
Ms. Mariela, do you know
who this woman with Caloy is?

153
00:09:36,284 --> 00:09:37,743
That's my 'Bi.

154
00:09:37,827 --> 00:09:38,953
'Bi?

155
00:09:43,332 --> 00:09:44,458
Abi?

156
00:09:46,544 --> 00:09:47,837
Is Abi your daughter?

157
00:09:48,921 --> 00:09:51,882
Ah, that's not Abi.

158
00:09:51,966 --> 00:09:54,385
That's Bea. She's my daughter.

159
00:09:55,052 --> 00:09:58,347
Bea? The one you were looking for here?

160
00:09:58,431 --> 00:09:59,724
Yes.

161
00:09:59,807 --> 00:10:02,476
But Abi is also my daughter.

162
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:05,396
But she's gone. She passed away.

163
00:10:05,479 --> 00:10:12,320
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

164
00:10:19,827 --> 00:10:20,870
[JORDAN] Yes, sir.

165
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:23,122
I stopped him from running away.

166
00:10:23,205 --> 00:10:25,333
We just wanted to know why he was there.

167
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:26,959
Why he was trespassing.

168
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:32,048
Based on records, Carlos Toledo
has a lot of pending cases.

169
00:10:32,131 --> 00:10:33,424
As of now, however,

170
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:35,551
we won't be able
to get a statement from him.

171
00:10:36,844 --> 00:10:38,304
I have to go and make a report for this.

172
00:10:38,387 --> 00:10:45,019
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

173
00:10:48,230 --> 00:10:50,274
[MARIELA] You can park there.
There you go.

174
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:53,903
We'll be right behind you, Ms. Mariela.

175
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:55,780
Okay. I'll wait for you.

176
00:10:57,948 --> 00:10:59,367
[LINE RINGS]

177
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:00,660
[PHONE RINGS]

178
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,081
Dude.

179
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:06,415
Hello, Jordan?

180
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:08,542
How's everything there?
How's it going with Caloy?

181
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:11,295
He's still unconscious.

182
00:11:12,046 --> 00:11:13,756
But I've talked to the police.

183
00:11:13,839 --> 00:11:15,925
Okay. Let's keep each other posted.

184
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:18,552
Are you sure
about what you're going to do?

185
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:22,181
Don't worry, Auntie Pres is with me.

186
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:23,682
Be safe.

187
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:25,226
Okay.

188
00:11:28,896 --> 00:11:34,777
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:11:50,709 --> 00:11:52,586
Come on, have a seat.

190
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:54,755
Make yourselves comfortable.

191
00:11:54,839 --> 00:11:58,467
Here. Drink it while it's hot.

192
00:11:58,551 --> 00:11:59,677
Thank you.

193
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:04,598
This is Abi.

194
00:12:04,682 --> 00:12:06,142
She's my eldest child.

195
00:12:06,225 --> 00:12:08,185
And this one here is Bea.

196
00:12:08,269 --> 00:12:10,938
She's the one who I thought
was working for you.

197
00:12:11,021 --> 00:12:12,648
[CHUCKLES]

198
00:12:13,858 --> 00:12:18,070
I apologize for how I behaved earlier.

199
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:21,699
Now I know why you
didn't know who Bea was.

200
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:23,534
I just don't understand

201
00:12:23,617 --> 00:12:26,454
why she didn't tell you her real name.

202
00:12:26,537 --> 00:12:28,080
I can't believe that kid.

203
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:31,792
I lost my temper when I saw that guy.

204
00:12:32,376 --> 00:12:36,297
I feel like he's a bad influence
on my daughter.

205
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:40,718
I won't let my daughter leave me
for that kind of man.

206
00:12:42,803 --> 00:12:45,931
Oh. Drink these before they get cold.

207
00:12:46,724 --> 00:12:49,351
No need to be shy.

208
00:12:49,435 --> 00:12:51,103
[PHONE CHIMES]

209
00:12:54,356 --> 00:12:56,567
MA, I'M ON MY WAY HOME.

210
00:12:56,650 --> 00:12:59,653
Perfect! Bea's on her way home.

211
00:12:59,737 --> 00:13:02,114
She always brings home food.

212
00:13:02,198 --> 00:13:04,658
It's always too much for the two of us.

213
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:06,118
So eat with us, okay?

214
00:13:06,202 --> 00:13:10,289
- [LINE RINGING]
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

215
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:24,803
Ms. Mariela, has it been a long time
since they met? Caloy and…

216
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:27,056
Bea.

217
00:13:27,139 --> 00:13:28,599
That was what Bea told me.

218
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:31,060
But I saw him for the first time
the other day.

219
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:34,271
How do you and Bea know each other?

220
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:36,315
Ah…

221
00:13:36,398 --> 00:13:38,192
She met her at Angels of Grace.

222
00:13:38,275 --> 00:13:41,362
Your daughter was there, and uh…

223
00:13:41,445 --> 00:13:44,031
Billy was a volunteer on that day.

224
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:47,701
That is why she has your calling card.

225
00:13:47,785 --> 00:13:51,914
I thought that was where she worked.

226
00:13:51,997 --> 00:13:53,082
Hmm…

227
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:59,338
Why does Bea always go to Angels of Grace?

228
00:14:02,591 --> 00:14:04,385
I'm making her worry, aren't I?

229
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:06,929
Your daughter loves you.

230
00:14:09,056 --> 00:14:12,017
Bea's an ambitious kid.

231
00:14:12,101 --> 00:14:14,687
She wants to be like her sister

232
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:17,273
and her idol.

233
00:14:17,356 --> 00:14:20,651
You see, there's a person she idolizes.

234
00:14:20,734 --> 00:14:23,404
She said that person
is a boss of her own company.

235
00:14:23,487 --> 00:14:27,157
She's always talking about her idol.

236
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:31,495
She was so happy that they became friends.

237
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:33,497
Is it you?

238
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:41,964
Bea kept talking
about how pretty her idol is

239
00:14:42,923 --> 00:14:44,508
and that she also has good skin!

240
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:46,552
And it perfectly describes you.

241
00:14:46,635 --> 00:14:48,470
You're her idol, aren't you?

242
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:51,849
Stay a bit more, okay?

243
00:14:51,932 --> 00:14:54,143
Let's wait for my daughter to arrive.

244
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:56,478
She'll be so happy when she sees you.

245
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:58,939
Can we take a selfie?

246
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:00,024
Selfie.

247
00:15:00,107 --> 00:15:02,902
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

248
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:06,697
[MARIELA] Mm! You smell so nice!
You even smell rich!

249
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:09,199
- No…
- Come on, smile.

250
00:15:09,742 --> 00:15:10,993
[CAMERA SHUTTERS CLICKING]

251
00:15:11,076 --> 00:15:14,204
That's it! So pretty!

252
00:15:14,788 --> 00:15:15,748
There.

253
00:15:15,831 --> 00:15:18,250
[MARIELA] I'm a fan now too!

254
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:20,294
Madam…

255
00:15:20,377 --> 00:15:22,755
Madam Billy. CEO.

256
00:15:22,838 --> 00:15:24,381
Ma'am Billy.

257
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:26,050
Just call me Billy, Ms. Mariela.

258
00:15:26,133 --> 00:15:27,426
[MARIELA GIGGLES]

259
00:15:27,509 --> 00:15:29,011
Oh, hold on.

260
00:15:30,012 --> 00:15:31,639
Just a second.

261
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:35,059
There's something I want to give you.

262
00:15:35,643 --> 00:15:37,603
This is a nice color.

263
00:15:37,686 --> 00:15:38,896
Look.

264
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:42,942
- This will look perfect on you.
- No, it's okay--

265
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:44,860
- Come on, just try it.
- No, you can--

266
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:47,196
Come on. Here you go.

267
00:15:47,279 --> 00:15:50,032
Okay, Ms. Mariela. I'll keep it.

268
00:15:50,115 --> 00:15:51,992
- Okay.
- Thank you.

269
00:15:52,076 --> 00:15:54,620
- Promise you'll wear it.
- Thank you.

270
00:15:55,871 --> 00:15:57,498
- [BILLY CLEARS THROAT]
- [MARIELA] Uh…

271
00:15:58,123 --> 00:16:00,501
I want to be friends with you too.

272
00:16:00,584 --> 00:16:02,044
Okay?

273
00:16:02,127 --> 00:16:03,253
And Precious,

274
00:16:03,337 --> 00:16:06,548
why didn't you tell me
your daughter was such a big shot?

275
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:08,384
You know,

276
00:16:09,677 --> 00:16:11,637
you remind me of my Abi.

277
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:16,934
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

278
00:16:17,017 --> 00:16:18,936
[PHONE CHIMES]

279
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:24,775
MAKE THEM LEAVE. I'LL EXPLAIN LATER.

280
00:16:26,819 --> 00:16:28,112
Is that Bea?

281
00:16:28,195 --> 00:16:29,989
Um…

282
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:33,158
I'm sorry, but she said
she'll be home late.

283
00:16:33,242 --> 00:16:35,577
She has something
she needs to take care of.

284
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:39,498
I guess there won't
be any dinner after all.

285
00:16:39,581 --> 00:16:41,667
But I could always order something.

286
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:43,335
No, that's okay.

287
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:45,254
We should get going anyway.

288
00:16:45,337 --> 00:16:48,257
- Thank you.
- Thank you, Mariela.

289
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:52,970
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

290
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:54,221
[CAR BEEPS]

291
00:16:57,141 --> 00:17:03,439
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

292
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:04,857
[ENGINE STARTS]

293
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:09,403
Billy, let's go.

294
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:17,119
What are you waiting for? Let's go.

295
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:19,788
Bea's here, Auntie.

296
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:23,417
Let's go, please.

297
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:29,840
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

298
00:17:29,923 --> 00:17:31,008
[KNOCKING ON CAR DOOR]

299
00:17:31,633 --> 00:17:33,302
[PRECIOUS GASPS]

300
00:17:37,681 --> 00:17:39,308
- You left this behind.
- Oh.

301
00:17:41,685 --> 00:17:42,853
Thank you.

302
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:50,277
Let's go.

303
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:56,325
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

304
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:09,546
Promise me
you'll never talk to Billy again.

305
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:14,593
Don't talk to Precious either,
or anyone connected to Billy.

306
00:18:14,676 --> 00:18:16,887
I thought she was your idol.

307
00:18:18,097 --> 00:18:21,809
She used to be, but not anymore.

308
00:18:21,892 --> 00:18:25,395
Ever since I started working
for her company's competitor,

309
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:28,524
she's been trying to ruin my reputation.

310
00:18:28,607 --> 00:18:31,360
She's been badmouthing me to my boss.

311
00:18:31,443 --> 00:18:32,861
Is that so?

312
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:35,114
But she seemed so nice.

313
00:18:35,948 --> 00:18:37,741
She seemed nice?

314
00:18:37,825 --> 00:18:39,368
Her niceness is all just an act.

315
00:18:39,451 --> 00:18:41,954
Don't let her fool you.

316
00:18:42,037 --> 00:18:43,914
Goodness, she's so cunning.

317
00:18:43,997 --> 00:18:46,166
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

318
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:47,668
Come on, eat your food.

319
00:18:49,419 --> 00:18:51,797
Auntie Pres, please tell
Auntie Lydia I said thanks

320
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:53,757
for taking care of Oliver.

321
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:55,217
- Yes, you know…
- Thank you.

322
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:58,262
Just give her food, and she'll be happy.

323
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,348
You know, Auntie,

324
00:19:01,431 --> 00:19:04,059
I think she figured out
we were at her house.

325
00:19:04,143 --> 00:19:06,812
That's probably why
Abi didn't come home, right?

326
00:19:06,895 --> 00:19:08,105
Bea.

327
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,732
She said her name's Bea, Auntie Pres.

328
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:15,404
But her mother, Mariela,
doesn't seem to know

329
00:19:15,487 --> 00:19:18,740
what her daughter's been up to.

330
00:19:19,783 --> 00:19:24,163
I also don't understand
why she has to use her sister's identity.

331
00:19:24,997 --> 00:19:26,582
Is she hiding from someone?

332
00:19:26,665 --> 00:19:30,210
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

333
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:32,337
[MUSIC FADES]

334
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:36,800
[OLIVER] <i>I also want my parents</i>
<i>to be proud of me.</i>

335
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:40,387
<i>Sometimes, I imagine them</i>
<i>looking down from heaven,</i>

336
00:19:40,470 --> 00:19:41,722
<i>hoping I do well.</i>

337
00:19:41,805 --> 00:19:44,975
<i>And that's my inspiration to study harder.</i>

338
00:19:48,562 --> 00:19:50,063
[PHONE RINGING]

339
00:19:51,106 --> 00:19:51,982
Hello?

340
00:19:52,065 --> 00:19:53,692
[ZANDRO] <i>Well, Enrico?</i>

341
00:19:53,775 --> 00:19:55,402
<i>When are you going to pay me?</i>

342
00:19:55,485 --> 00:19:58,280
Didn't I tell you to give me some time?

343
00:19:58,363 --> 00:20:01,366
<i>Time? Do you think I'm stupid?!</i>

344
00:20:01,950 --> 00:20:06,455
<i>You think you're safe</i>
<i>because you're back in the Philippines?</i>

345
00:20:06,538 --> 00:20:09,791
<i>I can have people hunt you down there,</i>
<i>you bastard!</i>

346
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:11,210
Whoa, Oliver!

347
00:20:12,669 --> 00:20:13,712
Oliver!

348
00:20:14,922 --> 00:20:16,590
What's wrong? Hang on.

349
00:20:16,673 --> 00:20:18,175
Have some water.

350
00:20:18,258 --> 00:20:21,887
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

351
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:23,430
Take it slow.

352
00:20:23,513 --> 00:20:24,973
Let me check your sugar levels.

353
00:20:27,184 --> 00:20:28,268
I'm fine now.

354
00:20:28,352 --> 00:20:29,228
Are you sure?

355
00:20:29,311 --> 00:20:30,604
Yes, mister.

356
00:20:32,481 --> 00:20:33,732
- Oliver!
- Have some more.

357
00:20:34,399 --> 00:20:35,651
What happened?

358
00:20:36,443 --> 00:20:38,237
- I'm okay now.
- Really?

359
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:40,572
I think he's just tired from cleaning.

360
00:20:40,656 --> 00:20:42,115
His sugar levels are normal.

361
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,534
I'm okay now.

362
00:20:46,453 --> 00:20:47,913
- Are you sure?
- Thank you, sir.

363
00:20:47,996 --> 00:20:49,289
You're welcome.

364
00:20:54,544 --> 00:20:56,588
Ma, I've made your lunch.

365
00:20:56,672 --> 00:20:58,465
Just eat it later. I'm heading out now.

366
00:20:58,548 --> 00:21:00,592
- Okay.
- Uh…

367
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:02,928
And don't forget about
what we talked about last night.

368
00:21:03,011 --> 00:21:07,182
If Billy calls you and asks about me,
don't talk to her. Okay?

369
00:21:08,934 --> 00:21:11,144
Ma, I'm being serious.

370
00:21:11,228 --> 00:21:13,146
- Mm-hmm.
- [KNOCKING ON DOOR]

371
00:21:17,609 --> 00:21:18,944
[POLICE OFFICER] Bea Dominguez.

372
00:21:19,778 --> 00:21:21,947
Could you come with us
to the police station?

373
00:21:22,030 --> 00:21:27,869
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

374
00:21:32,207 --> 00:21:33,959
<i>By the way, where are your kids?</i>

375
00:21:34,042 --> 00:21:35,752
<i>I'm all alone now.</i>

376
00:21:35,836 --> 00:21:38,588
<i>Same here. If it weren't</i>
<i>for Oliver and Billy,</i>

377
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:40,841
<i>I'd be alone in life too.</i>

378
00:21:40,924 --> 00:21:42,718
<i>How did you end up living together anyway?</i>

379
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:44,803
<i>I'll collect the debt myself.</i>

380
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:48,640
<i>The puppet master</i>
<i>who's been manipulating Caloy</i>

381
00:21:48,724 --> 00:21:49,975
<i>is actually Abi?</i>

382
00:21:50,058 --> 00:21:51,226
<i>Or rather, Bea!</i>

383
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:53,895
[BILLY] <i>What we don't know right now</i>
<i>is what her motive is.</i>

384
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:55,564
<i>There's a deeper reason.</i>

385
00:21:55,647 --> 00:21:58,650
<i>I just met him at a karaoke bar</i>
<i>and sang a duet with him.</i>

386
00:21:58,734 --> 00:22:00,110
<i>I don't know him at all!</i>

387
00:22:00,193 --> 00:22:01,987
<i>Your relationship with Caloy?</i>

388
00:22:02,070 --> 00:22:03,655
<i>I believe that's counted as conspiracy.</i>

389
00:22:03,739 --> 00:22:05,866
<i>You forged the name. The address.</i>

390
00:22:05,949 --> 00:22:07,326
<i>The educational background.</i>

391
00:22:07,409 --> 00:22:08,785
<i>You faked everything.</i>

392
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:11,163
<i>Did I murder someone?</i>

393
00:22:11,246 --> 00:22:12,789
<i>You stole something.</i>

394
00:22:12,873 --> 00:22:15,000
- <i>You're just pretending.</i>
- [GROANS] <i>Ow!</i>

395
00:22:15,083 --> 00:22:17,002
<i>Why does she want to destroy Billy?</i>

396
00:22:17,586 --> 00:22:19,171
<i>For once, Bea,</i>

397
00:22:19,254 --> 00:22:20,630
<i>tell the truth.</i>

398
00:22:25,552 --> 00:22:27,304
<i>What did I ever do to you?</i>
